        "videos/14-anesthesia-unknown/G4.jpg"
      ],
      "imageAt": [
        0,
        0.455
      ],
      "seconds": 22.43,
      "text": "We know what the drugs bind to. We know the doses, to the milligram, and we know how to bring you back. What we cannot explain is the moment itself. Why does a molecule in your bloodstream make experience stop? The brain does not shut down under anesthesia. It stays active. It simply stops holding itself together as one conversation.",
