      ],
      "imageAt": [
        0,
        0.4
      ],
      "seconds": 32.45,
      "text": "Picture an orchestra. Anesthesia does not silence the musicians. It takes away the conductor. Every section keeps playing, and nothing arrives together, so there is no music, and no one listening. That is the leading idea. The parts stay awake, and the binding fails. Which raises the uncomfortable question underneath. If consciousness can be removed by interrupting a connection, then it was never a thing you have. It was something your brain keeps doing.",
